 "question": "Whether the Gemma 4 26B Q8 record lane returns the same answers when the same server configuration is started again. The lane's gates cover fresh-response validity, cache-zero and canaries; they have never covered output identity, so this was unmeasured rather than claimed.",
 "method": "Four fresh servers, identical settings, the frozen 12-prompt realistic suite at a 512-token natural completion cap. The suite requests temperature 0, top_p 1 and seed 1 through the chat API, so decoding is greedy; prompt hashes were compared to confirm the inputs were identical.",
 "finding": "No output is reproducible. Every pairwise comparison scores 0/12, and divergence begins early - as soon as character 26 on one prompt. This is not sampling and not a different prompt set.",
 "caveat": "The lane serves with speculative decoding (--spec-type draft-mtp, Q4_0 MTP draft verified by the Q8 target). This measurement cannot separate a nondeterministic speculative path from a nondeterministic target; a draftless arm would be needed to attribute it. What it does establish is that the deployed configuration is not reproducible.",
 "context": "For comparison on the same host and suite shape: vLLM's INT4 W4A16 route on Qwen3.5 is 12/12 across fresh servers, and llama.cpp's Q8 route on Qwen3.5-9B is 8/12. Gemma 4 26B Q8 on llama.cpp is 0/12.",
